From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:51:28 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zumapro-tegu: Add the GPU's
 levels to 890 MHz

With gpu-thermal throttling the GPU, add the 9a's GPU levels above 649
MHz: 723, 807, 850 and 890 MHz. The table's top, 940 MHz, stays out
until it has run on the 9a.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts   | 21 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
index 95dfe0fbd..d68fd18f8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
@@ -76,8 +76,9 @@ key-volume-up {
 
 	/*
 	 * The GPU's levels: the shader rates of the Pixel 9a's GPU DVFS table
-	 * up to 649 MHz, each with its paired L2 rate through the ACPM "gpu"
-	 * clock. The levels above, to 940 MHz, wait for a GPU thermal zone.
+	 * up to 890 MHz, each with its paired L2 rate through the ACPM "gpu"
+	 * clock; gpu-thermal throttles them from 85 C. 940 MHz, the table's
+	 * top, is left out until it has run on the 9a.
 	 */
 	gpu_opp: opp-table-gpu {
 		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
@@ -117,6 +118,22 @@ opp-580000000 {
 		opp-649000000 {
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <649000000>;
 		};
+
+		opp-723000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <723000000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-807000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <807000000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-850000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <850000000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-890000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <890000000>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	/* UFS VCC, switched by gpp0-1 as on stock. */
